' Legend
legend right
  <b>Template Method Pattern Components:</b>

  <b>Template Method:</b> Final method that defines
  the algorithm skeleton. Cannot be overridden.

  <b>Abstract Methods:</b> Steps that MUST be
  implemented by concrete classes (required variation).

  <b>Hook Methods:</b> Steps that MAY be overridden
  by concrete classes (optional variation). Have
  default implementations.

  <b>Concrete Methods:</b> Steps with shared
  implementation (invariant behavior).

  <b>Key Principles:</b>
  • <b>Hollywood Principle:</b> "Don't call us, we'll call you"
    Parent controls flow, calls child methods
  • <b>Inversion of Control:</b> Template orchestrates algorithm
  • <b>Code Reuse:</b> Common logic written once
  • <b>Open/Closed:</b> Easy to add new types (extend)
    without modifying existing code

  <b>Benefits:</b>
  ✓ Eliminates code duplication
  ✓ Enforces consistent algorithm structure
  ✓ Controlled variation points
  ✓ Easy to extend with new calculator types
endlegend

@enduml